A knocked-out tooth should not be placed in water because it can damage the delicate cells of the dental pulp, increasing the risk of infection and reducing the chance of successful reimplantation. Storing a knocked-out tooth in water can also lead to tissue damage and potential complications during the reimplantation process. Lastly, water can serve as a growth medium for bacteria, which can cause infection and further harm the tooth and surrounding tissues.
